   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "f is a product of x and the composite sqrt(ln(x^2 + 1)), so f'(x) = sqrt(ln(x^2 + 1)) + x d/dx[sqrt(ln(x^2 + 1))].",
         "mathjson": [
            "Power",
            [
               "Ln",
               [
                  "Add",
                  1,
                  [
                     "Power",
                     "x",
                     2
                  ]
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Rational",
               1,
               2
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The composite has three layers: the square root gives 1/(2 sqrt(ln(x^2 + 1))), the log gives 1/(x^2 + 1), and x^2 + 1 gives 2x. Cancelling the 2, the product is x / ((x^2 + 1) sqrt(ln(x^2 + 1))).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            "x",
